    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change enforces a disposable-email-domain blocklist, rejecting owner creation/update with **400** when the email's domain is `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, or `guerrillamail.com`.\n\nI implemented it in the shared `OwnerEmails.normalize` helper (`src/main/java/.../function/owner/OwnerEmails.java`), which both the POST path (`BuildOwner`) and PUT path (`ValidateOwner`) already call:\n\n- Added a `DISPOSABLE_DOMAINS` set with the three blocklisted domains.\n- After the existing syntax check and lower-casing, extract the domain and throw the existing `InvalidEmailException` if it's on the blocklist.\n\n`InvalidEmailException` is already wired to an escalation handler that responds `400 Bad Request` with a `ProblemDetail`, so no new exception, handler, or YAML was needed. The blocklist check runs on the already-normalized (lower-cased) address, so mixed-case domains like `X@MailInator.COM` are also caught.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsDisposableDomain` passes, and the full suite is green.",
